ious\", \"handles stress very well\", \"good at assessing weather conditions\", \"excellent computer skills\". Also B \"pretentious\", \"wrong tone\", \"grumpy\", \"uncooperative\". C \"100% reliable\", \"creates positive atmosphere\", \"makes correct decisions quickly\", \"difficulty communicating ideas\", \"egocentric\", \"not willing to further education\". D \"responds to unexpected events adequately\", \"concentrates very well\", \"solves problems extremely well\", \"takes responsibility seriously\", \"moody\", \"loner\", \"arrogant\", \"weak leadership\". A \"anticipates dangerous situations\", \"sees complex connections\", \"excellent spatial vision\", \"very good leadership qualities\", \"not good at taking criticism\", \"unorganized\".\n\nWe can argue that B's stress handling outweighs C's reliability because stress resilience is critical. Also B's technical competence is essential. C's lack of willingness to further education is a red flag for adaptability. So we shift to B.\n\nThus our vote: Candidate B.\n\nNow produce PUBLIC_MESSAGE and METADATA_JSON."}
